{
  "slug": "claude-code-survival-kit",
  "name": "Claude Code Survival Kit",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "10 slash commands and 3 agent definitions distilled from 6 months of daily Claude Code use. Not a framework -- just the patterns that survived: multi-agent build pipelines, parallel task dispatch, security audits, session handoffs, and more.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 agents** and **10 commands**.\n\n- **Agents** (3): `coder` (Implements code strictly from a provided plan), `planner` (Generates detailed implementation plans with file structure, function signatures, data flow, edge cases, test specifications, and acceptance criteria), `reviewer` (Token-efficient code review)\n- **Commands** (10): `build` (Three-phase build: Opus plans → Sonnet implements with tests → Opus reviews), `dispatch` (Plan-then-dispatch: discovers file:line targets before spawning agents), `fresh` (Save context and prepare a clean handoff for a new session), `handoff` (Write a structured handoff document capturing session state so the next session can continue without re-discovery), `init` (Initialize a new project with standard structure, Claude Code config, and git), `plan` (Explore, think, and output a structured plan before executing anything), `railway-preflight` (Pre-deploy readiness check for Railway), `security-audit` (Security and resilience audit for apps built with AI agents), and 2 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install claude-code-survival-kit@claude-community` from `rjspence3/claude-code-toolkit`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "agent": 3,
    "command": 10
  },
